<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<LightningComponentBundle xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <apiVersion>67.0</apiVersion>
    <isExposed>true</isExposed>
    <!--
        DISPLAY LABELS ONLY. masterLabel and description are what an admin reads in the Lightning App
        Builder palette, so they track the card title: "Recent Packages" to "Recent Portfolios" to
        "Portfolio Deals" and then, all on the same day (2026-08-17), to the settled "Property
        Packages" - the plural of the underlying object's own label. The two middle names are both
        RETRACTED, not merely superseded: "Portfolio Deals" collided with an Opportunity stage value
        named "Portfolio Deal" that was live at the time. That stage value HAS SINCE BEEN RETIRED
        (phase A2 of the Portfolio Deal rename, deployed), so entry 3 survives as HISTORY - it records
        how the settled name was reached, not a permanent ban. What outlasts the collision is that the
        two names answered DIFFERENT QUESTIONS: this card lists "which inbound broker emails arrived",
        while the retired stage described "which seller's deal bundle is this part of". The full
        correction chain and the reason all four names cost no schema edits are in recentPackages.js's
        header, which is authoritative on the label.

        The bundle's API name stays `recentPackages`, and Lead_Funnel.flexipage-meta.xml references it
        by that API name, never by masterLabel, so this is not a page-breaking change. Every API name
        behind the card also stays "Package" TODAY: getRecentPackages, RecentPackageRow,
        PropertyPackageController, PropertyPackageSelector, Property_Package__c. Carrying four label
        renames at zero schema cost is the whole return on that split, so do not "finish the rename"
        into the schema HERE. Re-pointing those API names is the rename program's job, done wholesale
        in one authorised phase - not a passing edit's.
    -->
    <masterLabel>Property Packages</masterLabel>
    <description>Multi-property broker emails that arrived most recently, newest first, with each package's broker and its live Lead and Opportunity counts. Intended for the Acquisition app's Lead Funnel tab.</description>
    <targets>
        <target>lightning__AppPage</target>
        <target>lightning__HomePage</target>
    </targets>
</LightningComponentBundle>
